* Input for the COBOL program generated from network.packet:
*
*   packet_builder gen examples/network.packet -l cobol -o out
*   cobc -free -x -o out/network out/network.cob
*   out/network examples/network.dat
*
* One packet per line: <Packet> <hex bytes> [path=value ...].
* Blank lines and lines starting with * are comments.

* An Ethernet frame carrying IPv4 and UDP (a DNS query)
Ethernet ffffffffffff0242ac110002080045000028000040004011b8acc0a80001c0a800c7cf080035001400001a2b01000001000000000000

* IPv4 with a TCP segment and an MSS option
Ipv4 4500002c000040004006b8b3c0a80001c0a800c7c001005012345678000000006002faf01c460000020405b4

* A DNS answer whose name is compressed
DnsMessage 1a2b81800001000100000000076578616d706c6503636f6d0000010001c00c0001000100000e1000045db8d822

* The same UDP header with its source port changed before re-encoding
Udp cf080035001400001a2b01000001000000000000 source_port=53

* Cut short: decoding reports `incomplete`
Ipv4 45000028000040
